Shared memory:
 - SystemV
 - SystemD (POSIX):
  + Named
  + Anonymous
 - File-mapping

SystemV:
 - No named filesystem, but having key and ID of segment
 - Segment in RAM, existed until shmctl(IPC_RMID)
 - ftok(), shmget(), shmat(), shmdt(), shmctl()

SystemD named:
 - Virtual named filesystem
 - RAM file (no disk involvement), existed until shm_unlink(SHM_NAME)
 - shm_open(), ftruncate(), mmap(), munmap(), close()

SystemD unnamed/anonymous:
 - No named filesystem
 - Segment in RAM, used for process using fork()
 - mmap(), munmap()

File-mapping:
 - File on DISK
 - file in disk, existed until unlink(FILE_PATH)
 - open(), ftruncate(), mmap(), munmap(), close()

Test:
# Buffer on virtual kernel filesystem (POSIX named)
vinh@vinh-Inspiron-15-3520:~$ cat /dev/shm/posix_shm 
Hello from POSIX named shared memory!
-> This is after ./w

vinh@vinh-Inspiron-15-3520:~$ cat /dev/shm/posix_shm 
cat: /dev/shm/posix_shm: No such file or directory
-> This is after ./r

# Buffer on special file (on SD card disk) (file-mapping)
vinh@vinh-Inspiron-15-3520:~/user_space/05_shared_memory/02_Code$ cat shared_data.dat 
Hello from File-mapping shared memory PID=1297971

vinh@vinh-Inspiron-15-3520:~/user_space/05_shared_memory/02_Code$ cat shared_data.dat 
cat: shared_data.dat: No such file or directory